  {
   "id": 2,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    80,
    270
   ],
   "size": [
    315,
    80
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 1,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Testing-only workflow for the sweep harness; hidden from the template browser. Based on dgx-monarch-ltx25-t2v, with only the changes needed for this test. The shape the official template ships and the base graph leaves out: sample at half the canvas, double the video latent with the spatial upscaler, then sample three more steps at the full canvas. The 22B DiT runs twice, so the render costs about twice the base and recovers the detail the base gives up. Separate AV Latent splits the packed pair, because the upscaler takes a plain video latent; the audio half skips the upscaler and re-enters stage 2 beside the upscaled video, which re-noises and re-samples both. Stage 2 runs the shorter schedule, which starts below 1.0 and so refines instead of building from noise. 640x352 doubles to 1280x704, and both stages keep an even row count at world 2. Adds ltx-2.5-latent-spatial-upscaler-x2-bf16-1.0.safetensors in models/latent_upscale_models."
   ],
   "title": "DGX Monarch | LTX 2.5 two stage text to video with sound"
  },
